{"jobs":[{"id":"5e655487-e0f9-4471-96fd-355b1f5e0185","title":"Bring Your Own Engineering Team","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco Office","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"New York Office","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York City "}}}],"publishedAt":"2024-11-29T18:23:17.289+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":false,"workplaceType":"OnSite","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/odewithanthropic/5e655487-e0f9-4471-96fd-355b1f5e0185","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/odewithanthropic/5e655487-e0f9-4471-96fd-355b1f5e0185/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>About Ode with Anthropic</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">How do you turn a decades-old dataset into an industry-leading medical coding agent? Teach an AI receptionist to book appointments in Spanish? Automatically generate working data connectors from API docs? Build agents that write, test, and deploy their own software packages?</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Anthropic is defining frontier AI. Ode is the team bringing frontier AI into practice.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are a team of experienced builders who care deeply about getting complex AI systems into production, with strong conviction about what makes them succeed. As Anthropic’s services venture, we tackle the hardest, most consequential AI problems for companies with real stakes, working closely with their Applied AI and Product teams to turn frontier technology into real world impact.<br /></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're backed by Anthropic, Blackstone, Hellman &amp; Friedman, Goldman Sachs, General Atlantic, Leonard Green &amp; Partners, Apollo Global Management, GIC, and Sequoia Capital.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're headquartered in SF with offices in NYC, Raleigh-Durham, and Dubai.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>About Bringing Your Own Engineering Team</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Some teams are just too good to break up. Maybe you co-founded a venture that's pivoting, maybe your team got caught in a reduction in force, or maybe you're looking for the next thing to build together. We already work in small pods: tight-knit teams of engineers working on a single project together. Joining Ode is a natural way to keep your team intact and shift your focus to building for clients with instant product-market fit. If you're part of an existing team of 2–5 engineers, we encourage you to apply to join Ode with Anthropic together.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>How It Works</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>One interview process.</strong> We'll arrange your interviews on the same day, with the same panel, against the same bar we hold every Ode engineer to.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>One offer.</strong> If we decide to move forward, we'll make offers to your whole team at the same time. You're each free to accept or decline individually — though we hope you'll all say yes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>One first project.</strong> We'll work to staff you on an engagement together.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>BYOT In Practice: Fabius</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In 2026, we were introduced to the Fabius team — a Y Combinator (W23) startup that had spent three years building AI to automate sales workflows. They had a track record of building complex AI systems, and they'd spent considerable time perfecting the craft of partnering closely with customers to make sure their solutions delivered results. The more we talked, the more we saw a team whose strengths mapped almost exactly to what we hire for. For Fabius, joining Ode was a natural way to focus on what they were best at — building AI-powered products — while staying together as a team.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>\"I was surprised how much autonomy Ode expected us to keep. Suddenly we had very interested, very motivated clients — and the same hard technical problems we used to grind through at Fabius. \" — Neil Madsen, Fabius Co-founder</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>\"When we spoke with Eddie and Chris, it felt like a bunch of founders hanging out. There was a certain expectation that the team itself was an asset, and Ode was specifically interested in protecting the way we were working together, rather than figuring out how to make everyone play a narrow role.\"  - Andy Day, Fabius Co-founder</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Who We hire</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We generally expect your team to fall into the categories of one of our existing engineering and PM roles — most commonly <strong>Software Engineer</strong>, <strong>Senior/Staff Software Engineer</strong> or <strong>Forward Deployed PM</strong>. Take a look at those JDs to see what we look for at the individual level. We evaluate teams holistically on top of that, but we expect every team member to clear a similar bar as all other Ode team members.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Software Engineer</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Forward Deployed Product Manager</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>Our Engineering Philosophy</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're opinionated about what works in production, and we write about it — from why most eval setups fail by collapsing everything into a single score, to why defaulting to chat interfaces limits AI's impact.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We have a distinct approach to building AI systems: applying standard software engineering discipline to the non-deterministic world of frontier AI. We design systems around testable hypotheses, curate durable data sets, and ensure what we ship keeps working long after we've handed it over.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">After shipping 30+ AI products, we have strong opinions on what makes AI products succeed and how to get them into production. We think you'll find it refreshing if you've seen how most companies approach AI.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>How Ode Is Different</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A typical engineer here ships two to three products per year and learns from dozens more. You have outsized autonomy on each product — but you won't have a year to polish a single system. The upside is constant time on the frontier of models and tooling, and a muscle for AI product development that's hard to build anywhere else.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Most engineers look back at this as the biggest growth period of their career. But it's possible you won't like it — we recommend using the interview process to hear what our team thinks.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Our Values</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Overdeliver</strong>: We are writing the playbook on how to create enterprise value with LLMs, and building our reputation as the world’s best applied AI team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Overuse AI:</strong> We obsessively explore and experiment with Claude to push the frontier of applied AI and share what we learn with our teammates.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Over”engineer” the Culture: </strong>We’re building a culture that attracts and retains top applied AI talent, and we stress test large decisions through the perspective of our world class builders.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Location</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>San Francisco, CA<br />New York, NY</strong><br />Work arrangement: 4 days in-person, Fridays remote.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Benefits</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">🏦 Competitive Compensation Package: Attractive salary aligned with your experience and skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">📈 401k with Matching: Invest in your future with our company-matched retirement plan.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">🌴 Unlimited PTO: Take the time you need to relax and rejuvenate.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">🏥 Exceptional Medical, Dental, and Vision Coverage: Comprehensive health benefits to keep you and your family healthy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">🚑 Health FSA: Manage out-of-pocket health expenses effectively.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">🚌 Commuter Benefits: Make your travel to work easier and more affordable.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">🏥 Life Insurance: Providing peace of mind for you and your loved ones.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">🎉 Team Events and Activities: Regular events to build camaraderie and a strong team spirit.</p></li></ul><h1><strong>Ready to join us?</strong></h1>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT ODE WITH ANTHROPIC\n\nHow do you turn a decades-old dataset into an industry-leading medical coding agent? Teach an AI receptionist to book appointments in Spanish? Automatically generate working data connectors from API docs? Build agents that write, test, and deploy their own software packages?\n\n\n\nAnthropic is defining frontier AI. Ode is the team bringing frontier AI into practice.\n\n\n\nWe are a team of experienced builders who care deeply about getting complex AI systems into production, with strong conviction about what makes them succeed. As Anthropic’s services venture, we tackle the hardest, most consequential AI problems for companies with real stakes, working closely with their Applied AI and Product teams to turn frontier technology into real world impact.\n\n\nWe're backed by Anthropic, Blackstone, Hellman & Friedman, Goldman Sachs, General Atlantic, Leonard Green & Partners, Apollo Global Management, GIC, and Sequoia Capital.\n\n\n\nWe're headquartered in SF with offices in NYC, Raleigh-Durham, and Dubai.\n\n\n\n\nABOUT BRINGING YOUR OWN ENGINEERING TEAM\n\nSome teams are just too good to break up. Maybe you co-founded a venture that's pivoting, maybe your team got caught in a reduction in force, or maybe you're looking for the next thing to build together. We already work in small pods: tight-knit teams of engineers working on a single project together. Joining Ode is a natural way to keep your team intact and shift your focus to building for clients with instant product-market fit. If you're part of an existing team of 2–5 engineers, we encourage you to apply to join Ode with Anthropic together.\n\n\n\n\nHOW IT WORKS\n\n - One interview process. We'll arrange your interviews on the same day, with the same panel, against the same bar we hold every Ode engineer to.\n\n - One offer. If we decide to move forward, we'll make offers to your whole team at the same time. You're each free to accept or decline individually — though we hope you'll all say yes.\n\n - One first project. We'll work to staff you on an engagement together.\n\n\n\n\nBYOT IN PRACTICE: FABIUS\n\nIn 2026, we were introduced to the Fabius team — a Y Combinator (W23) startup that had spent three years building AI to automate sales workflows. They had a track record of building complex AI systems, and they'd spent considerable time perfecting the craft of partnering closely with customers to make sure their solutions delivered results. The more we talked, the more we saw a team whose strengths mapped almost exactly to what we hire for. For Fabius, joining Ode was a natural way to focus on what they were best at — building AI-powered products — while staying together as a team.\n\n\n\n\"I was surprised how much autonomy Ode expected us to keep. Suddenly we had very interested, very motivated clients — and the same hard technical problems we used to grind through at Fabius. \" — Neil Madsen, Fabius Co-founder\n\n\n\n\"When we spoke with Eddie and Chris, it felt like a bunch of founders hanging out. There was a certain expectation that the team itself was an asset, and Ode was specifically interested in protecting the way we were working together, rather than figuring out how to make everyone play a narrow role.\"  - Andy Day, Fabius Co-founder\n\n\n\n\nWHO WE HIRE\n\nWe generally expect your team to fall into the categories of one of our existing engineering and PM roles — most commonly Software Engineer, Senior/Staff Software Engineer or Forward Deployed PM. Take a look at those JDs to see what we look for at the individual level. We evaluate teams holistically on top of that, but we expect every team member to clear a similar bar as all other Ode team members.\n\n - Software Engineer\n\n - Forward Deployed Product Manager\n   \n   \n\n\nOUR ENGINEERING PHILOSOPHY\n\nWe're opinionated about what works in production, and we write about it — from why most eval setups fail by collapsing everything into a single score, to why defaulting to chat interfaces limits AI's impact.\n\n\n\nWe have a distinct approach to building AI systems: applying standard software engineering discipline to the non-deterministic world of frontier AI. We design systems around testable hypotheses, curate durable data sets, and ensure what we ship keeps working long after we've handed it over.\n\n\n\nAfter shipping 30+ AI products, we have strong opinions on what makes AI products succeed and how to get them into production. We think you'll find it refreshing if you've seen how most companies approach AI.\n\n\n\n\nHOW ODE IS DIFFERENT\n\nA typical engineer here ships two to three products per year and learns from dozens more. You have outsized autonomy on each product — but you won't have a year to polish a single system. The upside is constant time on the frontier of models and tooling, and a muscle for AI product development that's hard to build anywhere else.\n\nMost engineers look back at this as the biggest growth period of their career. But it's possible you won't like it — we recommend using the interview process to hear what our team thinks.\n\n\n\n\nOUR VALUES\n\n - Overdeliver: We are writing the playbook on how to create enterprise value with LLMs, and building our reputation as the world’s best applied AI team.\n\n - Overuse AI: We obsessively explore and experiment with Claude to push the frontier of applied AI and share what we learn with our teammates.\n\n - Over”engineer” the Culture: We’re building a culture that attracts and retains top applied AI talent, and we stress test large decisions through the perspective of our world class builders.\n\n\n\n\nLOCATION\n\nSan Francisco, CA\nNew York, NY\nWork arrangement: 4 days in-person, Fridays remote.\n\n\n\n\nBENEFITS\n\n - 🏦 Competitive Compensation Package: Attractive salary aligned with your experience and skills.\n\n - 📈 401k with Matching: Invest in your future with our company-matched retirement plan.\n\n - 🌴 Unlimited PTO: Take the time you need to relax and rejuvenate.\n\n - 🏥 Exceptional Medical, Dental, and Vision Coverage: Comprehensive health benefits to keep you and your family healthy.\n\n - 🚑 Health FSA: Manage out-of-pocket health expenses effectively.\n\n - 🚌 Commuter Benefits: Make your travel to work easier and more affordable.\n\n - 🏥 Life Insurance: Providing peace of mind for you and your loved ones.\n\n - 🎉 Team Events and Activities: Regular events to build camaraderie and a strong team spirit.\n\n\nREADY TO JOIN US?","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"d93607e0-3e38-4a6f-a05e-f293d3f3bdf4","title":"Forward Deployed Product Manager (SF/NY)","department":"Product","team":"Product","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco Office","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"New York Office","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York City "}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-09-16T21:11:10.233+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":false,"workplaceType":"OnSite","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/odewithanthropic/d93607e0-3e38-4a6f-a05e-f293d3f3bdf4","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/odewithanthropic/d93607e0-3e38-4a6f-a05e-f293d3f3bdf4/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>About Ode with Anthropic</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">How do you turn a decades-old dataset into an industry-leading medical coding agent? Teach an AI receptionist to book appointments in Spanish? Automatically generate working data connectors from API docs? Build agents that write, test, and deploy their own software packages?</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Anthropic is defining frontier AI. Ode is the team bringing frontier AI into practice.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are a team of experienced builders who care deeply about getting complex AI systems into production, with strong conviction about what makes them succeed. As Anthropic’s services venture, we tackle the hardest, most consequential AI problems for companies with real stakes, working closely with their Applied AI and Product teams to turn frontier technology into real world impact.<br /></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're backed by Anthropic, Blackstone, Hellman &amp; Friedman, Goldman Sachs, General Atlantic, Leonard Green &amp; Partners, Apollo Global Management, GIC, and Sequoia Capital.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're headquartered in SF with offices in NYC, Raleigh-Durham, and Dubai.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>The Role</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our customers come to us with ambitious, often fuzzy goals — make content moderation faster, customer service cheaper and better, unlock new integrations, automate the workflows no one else can touch.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Your job is to turn those goals into AI-powered solutions that work in the real world, and to own the journey from first conversation to live system to real business impact.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a forward-deployed, full-stack product management role:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Part <strong>product manager</strong> - you decide what we build and why.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Part <strong>engagement manager</strong> - you're the primary face of Ode to the client.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Part <strong>delivery manager</strong> - you run the execution motion end-to-end.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Part “<strong>do whatever it takes\" operator</strong> - you jump into the gaps to keep things moving.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Shape what we build and why.</strong> Translate ambiguous business problems into crisp problem statements, user journeys, and success metrics - and work with customers to define what \"success\" actually means.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Help create demand, not just fulfill it.</strong> Jump in early, messy conversations where the project is still a vague idea. Help tease out real pain, sketch solution approaches live, and spot expansion opportunities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Turn messy problems into shipped solutions.</strong> Translate ambiguous needs into clear requirements, PRDs, and plans for engineers. Shape workflows, edge cases, and evaluation criteria for AI-powered systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own the client relationship end-to-end.</strong> Act as the customer's day-to-day strategic partner and primary point-of-contact, building trust across all levels of the organization and being candid about tradeoffs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Drive execution across multiple AI products.</strong> Run the day-to-day rhythm including planning, check-ins, risk tracking, and coordinating between clients, engineers, designers, and Ode teammates to keep work unblocked and on time.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Drive adoption and long-term impact.</strong> Work with client teams on rollout, enablement, and change management so the systems you build actually get used. Bring back insights that inform Ode's playbooks and product direction.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Bring judgment and clarity.</strong> When requirements are fuzzy or customers change course, be the person in the room who can say: here's what we're trying to do, here's what we know, here's the plan.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>What You Bring</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Real product and delivery experience.</strong> You've built and shipped products with engineers and designers across multiple cycles. You love to execute and are good at it without building process for the sake of process.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Client-facing, high-stakes experience.</strong> You've led projects where clients were under pressure, stakeholders weren't aligned, and the path wasn't obvious. You're comfortable pushing back, reframing the problem, and holding the line on quality. We typically look for <strong>4+ years</strong> in product and consulting/client management or product implementations, operations, or support. However, we care more about what you've done than the label on your resume.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Structured problem-solving and communication.</strong> You ask good questions, structure chaos, and turn ambiguity into a plan - moving from whiteboarding with execs to writing a crisp doc for engineers without losing the plot. You are a clear and direct communicator.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Bias for action and ownership.</strong> You roll up your sleeves and make things happen, whether that's writing a scrappy SQL query, creating a prototype, drafting a support playbook, or jumping into a last-minute exec demo.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Comfort with ambiguity and intensity.</strong> You like high-energy environments, messy problems, and \"we haven't done this before\" projects. You can juggle multiple client, keep priorities straight, and make good calls with incomplete information. When you don’t know how to do something, you take the initiative to</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>AI curiosity, not AI Dogma.</strong> You don't need deep AI expertise on day one - you do need strong reasoning, a desire to learn fast, no job too big/small mentality, and a willingness to overuse AI in your own workflow.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Team-first mentality</strong>. You lift others up and actively share best practices and seek to learn from others. You care about winning together.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>How Ode Is Different</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A typical PM here ships two to three products per year and learns from dozens more. You have outsized autonomy on each product but you won't have a year to polish a single system. The upside is constant time on the frontier of models and tooling, and a muscle for AI product development that's hard to build anywhere else.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Many PMs look back at this as the biggest growth period of their career. But it's possible you won't like it and we recommend using the interview process to hear what our team members think.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Our Values</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Overdeliver</strong>: We are writing the playbook on how to create enterprise value with LLMs, and building our reputation as the world’s best applied AI team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Overuse AI:</strong> We obsessively explore and experiment with Claude to push the frontier of applied AI and share what we learn with our teammates.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Over”engineer” the Culture:</strong> We’re building a culture that attracts and retains top applied AI talent, and we stress test large decisions through the perspective of our world class builders.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div></li></ul><h1><strong>Location</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>San Francisco, CA</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work Arrangement: 4 days in-person, Fridays remote</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Benefits</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">🏦 Competitive Compensation Package: Attractive salary aligned with your experience and skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">📈 401k with Matching: Invest in your future with our company-matched retirement plan.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">🌴 Unlimited PTO: Take the time you need to relax and rejuvenate.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">🏥 Exceptional Medical, Dental, and Vision Coverage: Comprehensive health benefits to keep you and your family healthy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">🚑 Health FSA: Manage out-of-pocket health expenses effectively.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">🚌 Commuter Benefits: Make your travel to work easier and more affordable.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">🏥 Life Insurance: Providing peace of mind for you and your loved ones.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">🎉 Team Events and Activities: Regular events to build camaraderie and a strong team spirit.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Ready to join us?</strong></h1>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT ODE WITH ANTHROPIC\n\nHow do you turn a decades-old dataset into an industry-leading medical coding agent? Teach an AI receptionist to book appointments in Spanish? Automatically generate working data connectors from API docs? Build agents that write, test, and deploy their own software packages?\n\n\n\nAnthropic is defining frontier AI. Ode is the team bringing frontier AI into practice.\n\n\n\nWe are a team of experienced builders who care deeply about getting complex AI systems into production, with strong conviction about what makes them succeed. As Anthropic’s services venture, we tackle the hardest, most consequential AI problems for companies with real stakes, working closely with their Applied AI and Product teams to turn frontier technology into real world impact.\n\n\nWe're backed by Anthropic, Blackstone, Hellman & Friedman, Goldman Sachs, General Atlantic, Leonard Green & Partners, Apollo Global Management, GIC, and Sequoia Capital.\n\n\n\nWe're headquartered in SF with offices in NYC, Raleigh-Durham, and Dubai.\n\n\n\n\nTHE ROLE\n\nOur customers come to us with ambitious, often fuzzy goals — make content moderation faster, customer service cheaper and better, unlock new integrations, automate the workflows no one else can touch.\n\nYour job is to turn those goals into AI-powered solutions that work in the real world, and to own the journey from first conversation to live system to real business impact.\n\nThis is a forward-deployed, full-stack product management role:\n\n - Part product manager - you decide what we build and why.\n\n - Part engagement manager - you're the primary face of Ode to the client.\n\n - Part delivery manager - you run the execution motion end-to-end.\n\n - Part “do whatever it takes\" operator - you jump into the gaps to keep things moving.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Shape what we build and why. Translate ambiguous business problems into crisp problem statements, user journeys, and success metrics - and work with customers to define what \"success\" actually means.\n\n - Help create demand, not just fulfill it. Jump in early, messy conversations where the project is still a vague idea. Help tease out real pain, sketch solution approaches live, and spot expansion opportunities.\n\n - Turn messy problems into shipped solutions. Translate ambiguous needs into clear requirements, PRDs, and plans for engineers. Shape workflows, edge cases, and evaluation criteria for AI-powered systems.\n\n - Own the client relationship end-to-end. Act as the customer's day-to-day strategic partner and primary point-of-contact, building trust across all levels of the organization and being candid about tradeoffs.\n\n - Drive execution across multiple AI products. Run the day-to-day rhythm including planning, check-ins, risk tracking, and coordinating between clients, engineers, designers, and Ode teammates to keep work unblocked and on time.\n\n - Drive adoption and long-term impact. Work with client teams on rollout, enablement, and change management so the systems you build actually get used. Bring back insights that inform Ode's playbooks and product direction.\n\n - Bring judgment and clarity. When requirements are fuzzy or customers change course, be the person in the room who can say: here's what we're trying to do, here's what we know, here's the plan.\n   \n   \n\n\nWHAT YOU BRING\n\n - Real product and delivery experience. You've built and shipped products with engineers and designers across multiple cycles. You love to execute and are good at it without building process for the sake of process.\n\n - Client-facing, high-stakes experience. You've led projects where clients were under pressure, stakeholders weren't aligned, and the path wasn't obvious. You're comfortable pushing back, reframing the problem, and holding the line on quality. We typically look for 4+ years in product and consulting/client management or product implementations, operations, or support. However, we care more about what you've done than the label on your resume.\n\n - Structured problem-solving and communication. You ask good questions, structure chaos, and turn ambiguity into a plan - moving from whiteboarding with execs to writing a crisp doc for engineers without losing the plot. You are a clear and direct communicator.\n\n - Bias for action and ownership. You roll up your sleeves and make things happen, whether that's writing a scrappy SQL query, creating a prototype, drafting a support playbook, or jumping into a last-minute exec demo.\n\n - Comfort with ambiguity and intensity. You like high-energy environments, messy problems, and \"we haven't done this before\" projects. You can juggle multiple client, keep priorities straight, and make good calls with incomplete information. When you don’t know how to do something, you take the initiative to\n\n - AI curiosity, not AI Dogma. You don't need deep AI expertise on day one - you do need strong reasoning, a desire to learn fast, no job too big/small mentality, and a willingness to overuse AI in your own workflow.\n\n - Team-first mentality. You lift others up and actively share best practices and seek to learn from others. You care about winning together.\n   \n   \n\n\nHOW ODE IS DIFFERENT\n\nA typical PM here ships two to three products per year and learns from dozens more. You have outsized autonomy on each product but you won't have a year to polish a single system. The upside is constant time on the frontier of models and tooling, and a muscle for AI product development that's hard to build anywhere else.\n\nMany PMs look back at this as the biggest growth period of their career. But it's possible you won't like it and we recommend using the interview process to hear what our team members think.\n\n\n\n\nOUR VALUES\n\n - Overdeliver: We are writing the playbook on how to create enterprise value with LLMs, and building our reputation as the world’s best applied AI team.\n\n - Overuse AI: We obsessively explore and experiment with Claude to push the frontier of applied AI and share what we learn with our teammates.\n\n - Over”engineer” the Culture: We’re building a culture that attracts and retains top applied AI talent, and we stress test large decisions through the perspective of our world class builders.\n   \n    \n\n\nLOCATION\n\nSan Francisco, CA\n\nWork Arrangement: 4 days in-person, Fridays remote\n\n \n\n\nBENEFITS\n\n - 🏦 Competitive Compensation Package: Attractive salary aligned with your experience and skills.\n\n - 📈 401k with Matching: Invest in your future with our company-matched retirement plan.\n\n - 🌴 Unlimited PTO: Take the time you need to relax and rejuvenate.\n\n - 🏥 Exceptional Medical, Dental, and Vision Coverage: Comprehensive health benefits to keep you and your family healthy.\n\n - 🚑 Health FSA: Manage out-of-pocket health expenses effectively.\n\n - 🚌 Commuter Benefits: Make your travel to work easier and more affordable.\n\n - 🏥 Life Insurance: Providing peace of mind for you and your loved ones.\n\n - 🎉 Team Events and Activities: Regular events to build camaraderie and a strong team spirit.\n\n \n\n\nREADY TO JOIN US?","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$200K – $275K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$200K - $275K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"1579060a-f044-40d9-8f67-037994c1db4a","tierSummary":"The estimated total cash compensation range for this role is: $200K – $275K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"500d7c32-7e0b-4fd7-a7aa-cd2a57dc071b","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"6fe033d0-081b-402a-bece-4ab9d8a8e550","summary":"The estimated total cash compensation range for this role is: $200K – $275K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":200000,"maxValue":275000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":200000,"maxValue":275000}]}},{"id":"e2cd283d-72cb-4293-8095-15a0cde0e292","title":"Principal, AI Transformation","department":"Commercial","team":"Commercial","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco Office","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"Raleigh-Durham-Chapel Hill Area","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"North Carolina","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Raleigh"}}},{"location":"New York Office","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York City "}}}],"publishedAt":"2025-12-01T18:22:34.330+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":false,"workplaceType":"OnSite","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/odewithanthropic/e2cd283d-72cb-4293-8095-15a0cde0e292","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/odewithanthropic/e2cd283d-72cb-4293-8095-15a0cde0e292/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>About Ode with Anthropic</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">How do you turn a decades-old dataset into an industry-leading medical coding agent? Teach an AI receptionist to book appointments in Spanish? Automatically generate working data connectors from API docs? Build agents that write, test, and deploy their own software packages?</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Anthropic is defining frontier AI. Ode is the team bringing frontier AI into practice.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are a team of experienced builders who care deeply about getting complex AI systems into production, with strong conviction about what makes them succeed. As Anthropic’s services venture, we tackle the hardest, most consequential AI problems for companies with real stakes, working closely with their Applied AI and Product teams to turn frontier technology into real world impact.<br /></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're backed by Anthropic, Blackstone, Hellman &amp; Friedman, Goldman Sachs, General Atlantic, Leonard Green &amp; Partners, Apollo Global Management, GIC, and Sequoia Capital.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're headquartered in SF with offices in NYC, Raleigh-Durham, and Dubai.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>The Role</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're the call a CEO makes when they're ready to lead their industry into the age of AI — and the Principal is who answers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Think of this function as a fractional Chief AI Transformation Officer for our clients. The expectation is for you to become the CEO's right hand and trusted confidant — the primary executive counterpart who helps them move their company into the AI era from a position of strength. It's a role closer to a partner at a top firm than a typical sales or delivery seat.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll own the full arc. You win the business, embed with the CEO to find where AI changes the game, and mobilize a team of world-class PMs and engineers to deliver results — not slideware. Our Principals drive the company's revenue, and they earn it on insight and Applied AI expertise.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Win the business.</strong> Convert warm, high-intent executive relationships — sourced through our consortium and Anthropic — into signed engagements. Bring the judgment to qualify hard, the credibility to earn trust fast, and the finesse to negotiate and close.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Become the CEO's fractional Chief AI Transformation Officer.</strong> Embed with leadership as their trusted advisor on AI, diagnosing where the real opportunity is and shaping a path the business will actually act on.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Mobilize delivery.</strong> Stand up engagements quickly and keep them pointed at outcomes. We're more Palantir than McKinsey — you orchestrate the work that ships value, not decks that sit on a shelf.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own and grow the relationship.</strong> Stay the executive counterpart well past the first project, deepening trust and expanding the partnership over time.</p></li></ul><h1><strong>What You Bring</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You earn executive trust fast.</strong> CEOs and their leadership teams come to see you as the right hand they call first. You're crisp and compelling in the room and on the page, with any audience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Relentless learning agility and unmatched curiosity.</strong> You have a track record of ramping quickly and becoming an expert across a wide range of technical and industry topics. You don't need to be an Applied AI expert on day one — you do need the curiosity and horsepower to become an expert within 90 days, engage technical leaders as a peer, and turn pattern-matching across many engagements into a compounding advantage.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Strategic and business acumen.</strong> You see where AI creates real enterprise value and translate it into a path a business will move on.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You're relationship-driven.</strong> You build durable, high-trust relationships and own them for the long term — through the engagement and well beyond.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You're a partner teams want.</strong> Engineers and PMs are genuinely glad to have you in the room. You bring senior judgment and help resolve blockers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Revenue instinct.</strong> You recognize the right moments to advance and win business, and you have the commercial drive, urgency and finesse to close.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>Our Values</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Overdeliver</strong>: We are writing the playbook on how to create enterprise value with LLMs, and building our reputation as the world’s best applied AI team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Overuse AI:</strong> We obsessively explore and experiment with Claude to push the frontier of applied AI and share what we learn with our teammates.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Over”engineer” the Culture: </strong>We’re building a culture that attracts and retains top applied AI talent, and we stress test large decisions through the perspective of our world class builders.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div></li></ul><h1><strong>Location</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>San Francisco, CA</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work Arrangement: 4 days in-person, Fridays remote</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Benefits</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">🏦 Competitive Compensation Package: Attractive salary aligned with your experience and skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">📈 401k with Matching: Invest in your future with our company-matched retirement plan.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">🌴 Unlimited PTO: Take the time you need to relax and rejuvenate.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">🏥 Exceptional Medical, Dental, and Vision Coverage: Comprehensive health benefits to keep you and your family healthy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">🚑 Health FSA: Manage out-of-pocket health expenses effectively.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">🚌 Commuter Benefits: Make your travel to work easier and more affordable.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">🏥 Life Insurance: Providing peace of mind for you and your loved ones.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">🎉 Team Events and Activities: Regular events to build camaraderie and a strong team spirit.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Ready to join us?</strong></h1>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT ODE WITH ANTHROPIC\n\nHow do you turn a decades-old dataset into an industry-leading medical coding agent? Teach an AI receptionist to book appointments in Spanish? Automatically generate working data connectors from API docs? Build agents that write, test, and deploy their own software packages?\n\n\n\nAnthropic is defining frontier AI. Ode is the team bringing frontier AI into practice.\n\n\n\nWe are a team of experienced builders who care deeply about getting complex AI systems into production, with strong conviction about what makes them succeed. As Anthropic’s services venture, we tackle the hardest, most consequential AI problems for companies with real stakes, working closely with their Applied AI and Product teams to turn frontier technology into real world impact.\n\n\nWe're backed by Anthropic, Blackstone, Hellman & Friedman, Goldman Sachs, General Atlantic, Leonard Green & Partners, Apollo Global Management, GIC, and Sequoia Capital.\n\n\n\nWe're headquartered in SF with offices in NYC, Raleigh-Durham, and Dubai.\n\n\n\n\nTHE ROLE\n\nWe're the call a CEO makes when they're ready to lead their industry into the age of AI — and the Principal is who answers.\n\n\n\nThink of this function as a fractional Chief AI Transformation Officer for our clients. The expectation is for you to become the CEO's right hand and trusted confidant — the primary executive counterpart who helps them move their company into the AI era from a position of strength. It's a role closer to a partner at a top firm than a typical sales or delivery seat.\n\n\n\nYou'll own the full arc. You win the business, embed with the CEO to find where AI changes the game, and mobilize a team of world-class PMs and engineers to deliver results — not slideware. Our Principals drive the company's revenue, and they earn it on insight and Applied AI expertise.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Win the business. Convert warm, high-intent executive relationships — sourced through our consortium and Anthropic — into signed engagements. Bring the judgment to qualify hard, the credibility to earn trust fast, and the finesse to negotiate and close.\n\n - Become the CEO's fractional Chief AI Transformation Officer. Embed with leadership as their trusted advisor on AI, diagnosing where the real opportunity is and shaping a path the business will actually act on.\n\n - Mobilize delivery. Stand up engagements quickly and keep them pointed at outcomes. We're more Palantir than McKinsey — you orchestrate the work that ships value, not decks that sit on a shelf.\n\n - Own and grow the relationship. Stay the executive counterpart well past the first project, deepening trust and expanding the partnership over time.\n\n\nWHAT YOU BRING\n\n - You earn executive trust fast. CEOs and their leadership teams come to see you as the right hand they call first. You're crisp and compelling in the room and on the page, with any audience.\n\n - Relentless learning agility and unmatched curiosity. You have a track record of ramping quickly and becoming an expert across a wide range of technical and industry topics. You don't need to be an Applied AI expert on day one — you do need the curiosity and horsepower to become an expert within 90 days, engage technical leaders as a peer, and turn pattern-matching across many engagements into a compounding advantage.\n\n - Strategic and business acumen. You see where AI creates real enterprise value and translate it into a path a business will move on.\n\n - You're relationship-driven. You build durable, high-trust relationships and own them for the long term — through the engagement and well beyond.\n\n - You're a partner teams want. Engineers and PMs are genuinely glad to have you in the room. You bring senior judgment and help resolve blockers.\n\n - Revenue instinct. You recognize the right moments to advance and win business, and you have the commercial drive, urgency and finesse to close.\n   \n   \n\n\nOUR VALUES\n\n - Overdeliver: We are writing the playbook on how to create enterprise value with LLMs, and building our reputation as the world’s best applied AI team.\n\n - Overuse AI: We obsessively explore and experiment with Claude to push the frontier of applied AI and share what we learn with our teammates.\n\n - Over”engineer” the Culture: We’re building a culture that attracts and retains top applied AI talent, and we stress test large decisions through the perspective of our world class builders.\n   \n    \n\n\nLOCATION\n\nSan Francisco, CA\n\nWork Arrangement: 4 days in-person, Fridays remote\n\n \n\n\nBENEFITS\n\n - 🏦 Competitive Compensation Package: Attractive salary aligned with your experience and skills.\n\n - 📈 401k with Matching: Invest in your future with our company-matched retirement plan.\n\n - 🌴 Unlimited PTO: Take the time you need to relax and rejuvenate.\n\n - 🏥 Exceptional Medical, Dental, and Vision Coverage: Comprehensive health benefits to keep you and your family healthy.\n\n - 🚑 Health FSA: Manage out-of-pocket health expenses effectively.\n\n - 🚌 Commuter Benefits: Make your travel to work easier and more affordable.\n\n - 🏥 Life Insurance: Providing peace of mind for you and your loved ones.\n\n - 🎉 Team Events and Activities: Regular events to build camaraderie and a strong team spirit.\n\n \n\n\nREADY TO JOIN US?","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$300K – $600K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$300K - $600K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"c780face-0bbc-4eae-b6e8-1168193837e6","tierSummary":"The estimated compensation range for this role is $300K – $600K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"f40f695b-b151-4f0e-b111-71f3f83ca28f","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"7ffa79d6-2366-4667-82ff-6504a0146139","summary":"The estimated compensation range for this role is $300K – $600K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":300000,"maxValue":600000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":300000,"maxValue":600000}]}},{"id":"d1218507-6d99-4cfb-b7d5-cd34a633cda2","title":"Staff Software Engineer (NC)","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Raleigh-Durham-Chapel Hill Area","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-02-20T19:43:12.178+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":false,"workplaceType":"OnSite","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"North Carolina","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Raleigh"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/odewithanthropic/d1218507-6d99-4cfb-b7d5-cd34a633cda2","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/odewithanthropic/d1218507-6d99-4cfb-b7d5-cd34a633cda2/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>About Ode with Anthropic</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">How do you turn a decades-old dataset into an industry-leading medical coding agent? Teach an AI receptionist to book appointments in Spanish? Automatically generate working data connectors from API docs? Build agents that write, test, and deploy their own software packages?</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Anthropic is defining frontier AI. Ode is the team bringing frontier AI into practice.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are a team of experienced builders who care deeply about getting complex AI systems into production, with strong conviction about what makes them succeed. As Anthropic’s services venture, we tackle the hardest, most consequential AI problems for companies with real stakes, working closely with their Applied AI and Product teams to turn frontier technology into real world impact.<br /></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're backed by Anthropic, Blackstone, Hellman &amp; Friedman, Goldman Sachs, General Atlantic, Leonard Green &amp; Partners, Apollo Global Management, GIC, and Sequoia Capital.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're headquartered in SF with offices in NYC, Raleigh-Durham, and Dubai.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>The Role</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is designed for former engineering leaders (IC or EM) or founders who are comfortable owning end-to-end technical outcomes but specifically want to continue being impactful as individual contributors and spend more time in the code.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll work on a small, high-caliber team (2–5 engineers and a PM) building AI products for our clients. You'll set technical direction, write code, and be the person the team looks to when something is hard.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll spend roughly 75% of your time in code and 25% working directly with clients — often their CTOs — understanding problems, walking through tradeoffs, and making sure what we’re building meets their needs.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Most engineers take a decade to see this range of hard problems across this many domains. Here, you'll do it in your first year. To make this possible, we are religious about being the best company in the world to learn Applied AI engineering practices.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>What You Bring</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>8+ years of engineering experience, with deep care for the craft.</strong> You've shipped multiple complete products end-to-end and write elegant, production-ready code across multiple disciplines.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Specific interest in applying software engineering fundamentals to AI systems.</strong> You care about balancing frontier model capabilities with good system design.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Comfort talking with senior technical stakeholders.</strong> You navigate conversations skillfully, and care about people using what you build.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>High ownership mindset.</strong> You jump in without instruction, embrace a \"no job too big, no job too small\" mindset, and want to shape strategy and culture.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Low ego, high integrity.</strong> You help others and ask for help. You hold a high bar for honesty–with yourself and your team.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div></li></ul><h1><strong>Our Engineering Philosophy</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We have a distinct approach to building AI systems: applying standard software engineering discipline to the non-deterministic world of frontier AI. We design systems around testable hypotheses, curate durable data sets, and ensure what we ship keeps working long after we've handed it over.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">After shipping 30+ AI products, we have strong opinions on what makes AI products succeed and how to get them into production. We think you'll find it refreshing if you've seen how most companies approach AI.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>How Ode Is Different</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A typical engineer here ships two to three products per year and learns from dozens more. You have outsized autonomy on each product — but you won't have a year to polish a single system. The upside is constant time on the frontier of models and tooling, and a muscle for AI product development that's hard to build anywhere else.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Most engineers look back at this as the biggest growth period of their career. But it's possible you won't like it — we recommend using the interview process to hear what our engineers think.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Our Values</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Overdeliver</strong>: We are writing the playbook on how to create enterprise value with LLMs, and building our reputation as the world’s best applied AI team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Overuse AI:</strong> We obsessively explore and experiment with Claude to push the frontier of applied AI and share what we learn with our teammates.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Over”engineer” the Culture: </strong>We’re building a culture that attracts and retains top applied AI talent, and we stress test large decisions through the perspective of our world class builders.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div></li></ul><h1><strong>Location</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Raleigh-Durham-Chapel Hill, NC</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work Arrangement: 4 days in-person, Fridays remote</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Benefits</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">🏦 Competitive Compensation Package: Attractive salary aligned with your experience and skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">📈 401k with Matching: Invest in your future with our company-matched retirement plan.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">🌴 Unlimited PTO: Take the time you need to relax and rejuvenate.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">🏥 Exceptional Medical, Dental, and Vision Coverage: Comprehensive health benefits to keep you and your family healthy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">🚑 Health FSA: Manage out-of-pocket health expenses effectively.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">🚌 Commuter Benefits: Make your travel to work easier and more affordable.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">🏥 Life Insurance: Providing peace of mind for you and your loved ones.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">🎉 Team Events and Activities: Regular events to build camaraderie and a strong team spirit.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Ready to join us?</strong></h1>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT ODE WITH ANTHROPIC\n\n\n\nHow do you turn a decades-old dataset into an industry-leading medical coding agent? Teach an AI receptionist to book appointments in Spanish? Automatically generate working data connectors from API docs? Build agents that write, test, and deploy their own software packages?\n\n\n\nAnthropic is defining frontier AI. Ode is the team bringing frontier AI into practice.\n\n\n\nWe are a team of experienced builders who care deeply about getting complex AI systems into production, with strong conviction about what makes them succeed. As Anthropic’s services venture, we tackle the hardest, most consequential AI problems for companies with real stakes, working closely with their Applied AI and Product teams to turn frontier technology into real world impact.\n\n\nWe're backed by Anthropic, Blackstone, Hellman & Friedman, Goldman Sachs, General Atlantic, Leonard Green & Partners, Apollo Global Management, GIC, and Sequoia Capital.\n\n\n\nWe're headquartered in SF with offices in NYC, Raleigh-Durham, and Dubai.\n\n \n\n\nTHE ROLE\n\nThis role is designed for former engineering leaders (IC or EM) or founders who are comfortable owning end-to-end technical outcomes but specifically want to continue being impactful as individual contributors and spend more time in the code.\n\n \n\nYou'll work on a small, high-caliber team (2–5 engineers and a PM) building AI products for our clients. You'll set technical direction, write code, and be the person the team looks to when something is hard.\n\n \n\nYou'll spend roughly 75% of your time in code and 25% working directly with clients — often their CTOs — understanding problems, walking through tradeoffs, and making sure what we’re building meets their needs.\n\n \n\nMost engineers take a decade to see this range of hard problems across this many domains. Here, you'll do it in your first year. To make this possible, we are religious about being the best company in the world to learn Applied AI engineering practices.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU BRING\n\n - 8+ years of engineering experience, with deep care for the craft. You've shipped multiple complete products end-to-end and write elegant, production-ready code across multiple disciplines.\n\n - Specific interest in applying software engineering fundamentals to AI systems. You care about balancing frontier model capabilities with good system design.\n\n - Comfort talking with senior technical stakeholders. You navigate conversations skillfully, and care about people using what you build.\n\n - High ownership mindset. You jump in without instruction, embrace a \"no job too big, no job too small\" mindset, and want to shape strategy and culture.\n\n - Low ego, high integrity. You help others and ask for help. You hold a high bar for honesty–with yourself and your team.\n   \n    \n\n\nOUR ENGINEERING PHILOSOPHY\n\nWe have a distinct approach to building AI systems: applying standard software engineering discipline to the non-deterministic world of frontier AI. We design systems around testable hypotheses, curate durable data sets, and ensure what we ship keeps working long after we've handed it over.\n\n \n\nAfter shipping 30+ AI products, we have strong opinions on what makes AI products succeed and how to get them into production. We think you'll find it refreshing if you've seen how most companies approach AI.\n\n \n\n\nHOW ODE IS DIFFERENT\n\nA typical engineer here ships two to three products per year and learns from dozens more. You have outsized autonomy on each product — but you won't have a year to polish a single system. The upside is constant time on the frontier of models and tooling, and a muscle for AI product development that's hard to build anywhere else.\n\n \n\nMost engineers look back at this as the biggest growth period of their career. But it's possible you won't like it — we recommend using the interview process to hear what our engineers think.\n\n \n\n\nOUR VALUES\n\n - Overdeliver: We are writing the playbook on how to create enterprise value with LLMs, and building our reputation as the world’s best applied AI team.\n\n - Overuse AI: We obsessively explore and experiment with Claude to push the frontier of applied AI and share what we learn with our teammates.\n\n - Over”engineer” the Culture: We’re building a culture that attracts and retains top applied AI talent, and we stress test large decisions through the perspective of our world class builders.\n   \n    \n\n\nLOCATION\n\nRaleigh-Durham-Chapel Hill, NC\n\nWork Arrangement: 4 days in-person, Fridays remote\n\n \n\n\nBENEFITS\n\n - 🏦 Competitive Compensation Package: Attractive salary aligned with your experience and skills.\n\n - 📈 401k with Matching: Invest in your future with our company-matched retirement plan.\n\n - 🌴 Unlimited PTO: Take the time you need to relax and rejuvenate.\n\n - 🏥 Exceptional Medical, Dental, and Vision Coverage: Comprehensive health benefits to keep you and your family healthy.\n\n - 🚑 Health FSA: Manage out-of-pocket health expenses effectively.\n\n - 🚌 Commuter Benefits: Make your travel to work easier and more affordable.\n\n - 🏥 Life Insurance: Providing peace of mind for you and your loved ones.\n\n - 🎉 Team Events and Activities: Regular events to build camaraderie and a strong team spirit.\n\n \n\n\nREADY TO JOIN US?","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"f6665898-bf45-4cda-9246-4be5033f2082","title":"Associate Principal, AI Transformation","department":"Commercial","team":"Commercial","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco Office","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"New York Office","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York City "}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-04-03T00:07:17.453+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":false,"workplaceType":"OnSite","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/odewithanthropic/f6665898-bf45-4cda-9246-4be5033f2082","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/odewithanthropic/f6665898-bf45-4cda-9246-4be5033f2082/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>About Ode with Anthropic</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">How do you turn a decades-old dataset into an industry-leading medical coding agent? Teach an AI receptionist to book appointments in Spanish? Automatically generate working data connectors from API docs? Build agents that write, test, and deploy their own software packages?<br /></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Anthropic is defining frontier AI. Ode is the team bringing frontier AI into practice.<br /></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are a team of experienced builders who care deeply about getting complex AI systems into production, with strong conviction about what makes them succeed. As Anthropic’s services venture, we tackle the hardest, most consequential AI problems for companies with real stakes, working closely with their Applied AI and Product teams to turn frontier technology into real world impact.<br /></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're backed by Anthropic, Blackstone, Hellman &amp; Friedman, Goldman Sachs, General Atlantic, Leonard Green &amp; Partners, Apollo Global Management, GIC, and Sequoia Capital.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're headquartered in SF with offices in NYC, Raleigh-Durham, and Dubai.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>The Role</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The fastest way to learn how AI will reshape businesses is to go inside and help transform dozens of them. As an Associate Principal, you're the engine of our AI strategic advisory work — partnering with Principals to set companies' AI transformation agendas, and assessing value-creation opportunities and disruption risk across industries in diligence. In a given quarter you'll see inside several businesses and build pattern recognition that no other role in the market can offer.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is the path to becoming the “fractional Chief AI Transformation Officer” our clients call first. You'll work shoulder-to-shoulder with Principals on live engagements, proposals, and relationship building, taking on more of the selling motion as you go. The role is not quota-carrying today, but it's built to grow into one.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Drive AI strategic advisory engagements end-to-end.</strong> You run point strategic engagements that set a company's transformation agenda or running diligence on an asset</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Support live deals and the selling motion.</strong> Work alongside Principals on active pursuits — joining discovery calls, shaping proposals, helping manage relationships — and learn how we scope, price, and position our work.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build your network.</strong> Through engagements and deal support, build durable relationships with executives and investors.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Be a high-utility player.</strong> As an early-stage company, the work extends beyond any one engagement — you'll jump into adjacent streams like partnership development, thought leadership, or internal tooling and process improvement.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Bring</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>High ownership, comfort with ambiguity.</strong> Engagement windows are tight, and you drive the work forward without waiting to be told what to do.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Learning agility and analytical horsepower.</strong> You ramp quickly on an unfamiliar industry, identify what matters, and form a defensible point of view — turning pattern-matching across engagements into a compounding advantage.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Crisp communication, written and verbal.</strong> You translate technical AI concepts into business language that lands with executives and deal teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Relationship-building instinct.</strong> You build rapport with people and are energized, not drained, by client-facing work.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>AI-native.</strong> You're genuinely interested in AI and have a working understanding of what generative AI can and can't do. You don't need to be an engineer, but you need to be credible in a room with one.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Low ego, high resourcefulness.</strong> You're both a doer and a strategist.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>3-Month Snapshot</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You've contributed to several AI strategic advisory engagements alongside our Principals, progressing from supporting role to execution lead.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You're independently driving key takeaways, executive interviews, and deliverable creationn on active engagements.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You've joined live sales or account conversations with a Principal, and are starting to understand how we scope, price, and position our work.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You've identified at least one way to improve how we operate — process, tooling, templates — and started making it better.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Our Values</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Overdeliver</strong>: We are writing the playbook on how to create enterprise value with LLMs, and building our reputation as the world’s best applied AI team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Overuse AI:</strong> We obsessively explore and experiment with Claude to push the frontier of applied AI and share what we learn with our teammates.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Over”engineer” the Culture: </strong>We’re building a culture that attracts and retains top applied AI talent, and we stress test large decisions through the perspective of our world class builders.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Location</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>San Francisco, CA</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>New York City, NY</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work Arrangement: 4 days in-person, Fridays remote</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Benefits</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">🏦 Competitive Compensation Package: Attractive salary aligned with your experience and skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">📈 401k with Matching: Invest in your future with our company-matched retirement plan.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">🌴 Unlimited PTO: Take the time you need to relax and rejuvenate.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">🏥 Exceptional Medical, Dental, and Vision Coverage: Comprehensive health benefits to keep you and your family healthy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">🚑 Health FSA: Manage out-of-pocket health expenses effectively.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">🚌 Commuter Benefits: Make your travel to work easier and more affordable.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">🏥 Life Insurance: Providing peace of mind for you and your loved ones.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">🎉 Team Events and Activities: Regular events to build camaraderie and a strong team spirit.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>Ready to join us?</strong></h1>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT ODE WITH ANTHROPIC\n\nHow do you turn a decades-old dataset into an industry-leading medical coding agent? Teach an AI receptionist to book appointments in Spanish? Automatically generate working data connectors from API docs? Build agents that write, test, and deploy their own software packages?\n\n\nAnthropic is defining frontier AI. Ode is the team bringing frontier AI into practice.\n\n\nWe are a team of experienced builders who care deeply about getting complex AI systems into production, with strong conviction about what makes them succeed. As Anthropic’s services venture, we tackle the hardest, most consequential AI problems for companies with real stakes, working closely with their Applied AI and Product teams to turn frontier technology into real world impact.\n\n\nWe're backed by Anthropic, Blackstone, Hellman & Friedman, Goldman Sachs, General Atlantic, Leonard Green & Partners, Apollo Global Management, GIC, and Sequoia Capital.\n\n\n\nWe're headquartered in SF with offices in NYC, Raleigh-Durham, and Dubai.\n\n\n\n\nTHE ROLE\n\nThe fastest way to learn how AI will reshape businesses is to go inside and help transform dozens of them. As an Associate Principal, you're the engine of our AI strategic advisory work — partnering with Principals to set companies' AI transformation agendas, and assessing value-creation opportunities and disruption risk across industries in diligence. In a given quarter you'll see inside several businesses and build pattern recognition that no other role in the market can offer.\n\n\n\nThis is the path to becoming the “fractional Chief AI Transformation Officer” our clients call first. You'll work shoulder-to-shoulder with Principals on live engagements, proposals, and relationship building, taking on more of the selling motion as you go. The role is not quota-carrying today, but it's built to grow into one.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Drive AI strategic advisory engagements end-to-end. You run point strategic engagements that set a company's transformation agenda or running diligence on an asset\n\n - Support live deals and the selling motion. Work alongside Principals on active pursuits — joining discovery calls, shaping proposals, helping manage relationships — and learn how we scope, price, and position our work.\n\n - Build your network. Through engagements and deal support, build durable relationships with executives and investors.\n\n - Be a high-utility player. As an early-stage company, the work extends beyond any one engagement — you'll jump into adjacent streams like partnership development, thought leadership, or internal tooling and process improvement.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU BRING\n\n - High ownership, comfort with ambiguity. Engagement windows are tight, and you drive the work forward without waiting to be told what to do.\n\n - Learning agility and analytical horsepower. You ramp quickly on an unfamiliar industry, identify what matters, and form a defensible point of view — turning pattern-matching across engagements into a compounding advantage.\n\n - Crisp communication, written and verbal. You translate technical AI concepts into business language that lands with executives and deal teams.\n\n - Relationship-building instinct. You build rapport with people and are energized, not drained, by client-facing work.\n\n - AI-native. You're genuinely interested in AI and have a working understanding of what generative AI can and can't do. You don't need to be an engineer, but you need to be credible in a room with one.\n\n - Low ego, high resourcefulness. You're both a doer and a strategist.\n\n\n\n\n3-MONTH SNAPSHOT\n\n - You've contributed to several AI strategic advisory engagements alongside our Principals, progressing from supporting role to execution lead.\n\n - You're independently driving key takeaways, executive interviews, and deliverable creationn on active engagements.\n\n - You've joined live sales or account conversations with a Principal, and are starting to understand how we scope, price, and position our work.\n\n - You've identified at least one way to improve how we operate — process, tooling, templates — and started making it better.\n\n\n\n\nOUR VALUES\n\n - Overdeliver: We are writing the playbook on how to create enterprise value with LLMs, and building our reputation as the world’s best applied AI team.\n\n - Overuse AI: We obsessively explore and experiment with Claude to push the frontier of applied AI and share what we learn with our teammates.\n\n - Over”engineer” the Culture: We’re building a culture that attracts and retains top applied AI talent, and we stress test large decisions through the perspective of our world class builders.\n\n\n\n\nLOCATION\n\nSan Francisco, CA\n\nNew York City, NY\n\nWork Arrangement: 4 days in-person, Fridays remote\n\n\n\n\nBENEFITS\n\n - 🏦 Competitive Compensation Package: Attractive salary aligned with your experience and skills.\n\n - 📈 401k with Matching: Invest in your future with our company-matched retirement plan.\n\n - 🌴 Unlimited PTO: Take the time you need to relax and rejuvenate.\n\n - 🏥 Exceptional Medical, Dental, and Vision Coverage: Comprehensive health benefits to keep you and your family healthy.\n\n - 🚑 Health FSA: Manage out-of-pocket health expenses effectively.\n\n - 🚌 Commuter Benefits: Make your travel to work easier and more affordable.\n\n - 🏥 Life Insurance: Providing peace of mind for you and your loved ones.\n\n - 🎉 Team Events and Activities: Regular events to build camaraderie and a strong team spirit.\n\n \n\n\nREADY TO JOIN US?","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$200K – $250K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$200K - $250K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"451bd794-8851-4dd6-affe-0f25fd4bfd37","tierSummary":"$200K – $250K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"71297d9c-ebcb-4144-873d-a3b7dabd1d46","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"82332b43-b9f0-465a-8e6d-ec1490331646","summary":"$200K – $250K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":200000,"maxValue":250000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":200000,"maxValue":250000}]}},{"id":"22e6bcd3-b80d-462d-bd79-9deae131ee94","title":"Staff Software Engineer (SF/NY)","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco Office","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"South Bay Office","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":""}}},{"location":"New York Office","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York City "}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-04-28T23:41:10.216+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":false,"workplaceType":"OnSite","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/odewithanthropic/22e6bcd3-b80d-462d-bd79-9deae131ee94","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/odewithanthropic/22e6bcd3-b80d-462d-bd79-9deae131ee94/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>About Ode with Anthropic</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">How do you turn a decades-old dataset into an industry-leading medical coding agent? Teach an AI receptionist to book appointments in Spanish? Automatically generate working data connectors from API docs? Build agents that write, test, and deploy their own software packages?</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Anthropic is defining frontier AI. Ode is the team bringing frontier AI into practice.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are a team of experienced builders who care deeply about getting complex AI systems into production, with strong conviction about what makes them succeed. As Anthropic’s services venture, we tackle the hardest, most consequential AI problems for companies with real stakes, working closely with their Applied AI and Product teams to turn frontier technology into real world impact.<br /></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're backed by Anthropic, Blackstone, Hellman &amp; Friedman, Goldman Sachs, General Atlantic, Leonard Green &amp; Partners, Apollo Global Management, GIC, and Sequoia Capital.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're headquartered in SF with offices in NYC, Raleigh-Durham, and Dubai.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>The Role</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is designed for former engineering leaders (IC or EM) or founders who are comfortable owning end-to-end technical outcomes but specifically want to continue being impactful as individual contributors and spend more time in the code.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll work on a small, high-caliber team (2–5 engineers and a PM) building AI products for our clients. You'll set technical direction, write code, and be the person the team looks to when something is hard.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll spend roughly 75% of your time in code and 25% working directly with clients — often their CTOs — understanding problems, walking through tradeoffs, and making sure what we’re building meets their needs.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Most engineers take a decade to see this range of hard problems across this many domains. Here, you'll do it in your first year. To make this possible, we are religious about being the best company in the world to learn Applied AI engineering practices.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You Bring</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>8+ years of engineering experience, with deep care for the craft.</strong> You've shipped multiple complete products end-to-end and write elegant, production-ready code across multiple disciplines.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Specific interest in applying software engineering fundamentals to AI systems.</strong> You care about balancing frontier model capabilities with good system design.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Comfort talking with senior technical stakeholders.</strong> You navigate conversations skillfully, and care about people using what you build.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>High ownership mindset.</strong> You jump in without instruction, embrace a \"no job too big, no job too small\" mindset, and want to shape strategy and culture.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Low ego, high integrity.</strong> You help others and ask for help. You hold a high bar for honesty–with yourself and your team.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>Our Engineering Philosophy</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We have a distinct approach to building AI systems: applying standard software engineering discipline to the non-deterministic world of frontier AI. We design systems around testable hypotheses, curate durable data sets, and ensure what we ship keeps working long after we've handed it over.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">After shipping 30+ AI products, we have strong opinions on what makes AI products succeed and how to get them into production. We think you'll find it refreshing if you've seen how most companies approach AI.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>How Ode Is Different</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A typical engineer here ships two to three products per year and learns from dozens more. You have outsized autonomy on each product — but you won't have a year to polish a single system. The upside is constant time on the frontier of models and tooling, and a muscle for AI product development that's hard to build anywhere else.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Most engineers look back at this as the biggest growth period of their career. But it's possible you won't like it — we recommend using the interview process to hear what our engineers think.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Our Values</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Overdeliver</strong>: We are writing the playbook on how to create enterprise value with LLMs, and building our reputation as the world’s best applied AI team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Overuse AI:</strong> We obsessively explore and experiment with Claude to push the frontier of applied AI and share what we learn with our teammates.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Over”engineer” the Culture: </strong>We’re building a culture that attracts and retains top applied AI talent, and we stress test large decisions through the perspective of our world class builders.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>Location</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>San Francisco, CA<br />New York, NY</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work Arrangement: 4 days in-person, Fridays remote</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Benefits</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">🏦 Competitive Compensation Package: Attractive salary aligned with your experience and skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">📈 401k with Matching: Invest in your future with our company-matched retirement plan.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">🌴 Unlimited PTO: Take the time you need to relax and rejuvenate.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">🏥 Exceptional Medical, Dental, and Vision Coverage: Comprehensive health benefits to keep you and your family healthy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">🚑 Health FSA: Manage out-of-pocket health expenses effectively.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">🚌 Commuter Benefits: Make your travel to work easier and more affordable.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">🏥 Life Insurance: Providing peace of mind for you and your loved ones.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">🎉 Team Events and Activities: Regular events to build camaraderie and a strong team spirit.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Ready to join us?</strong></h1>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT ODE WITH ANTHROPIC\n\nHow do you turn a decades-old dataset into an industry-leading medical coding agent? Teach an AI receptionist to book appointments in Spanish? Automatically generate working data connectors from API docs? Build agents that write, test, and deploy their own software packages?\n\n\n\nAnthropic is defining frontier AI. Ode is the team bringing frontier AI into practice.\n\n\n\nWe are a team of experienced builders who care deeply about getting complex AI systems into production, with strong conviction about what makes them succeed. As Anthropic’s services venture, we tackle the hardest, most consequential AI problems for companies with real stakes, working closely with their Applied AI and Product teams to turn frontier technology into real world impact.\n\n\nWe're backed by Anthropic, Blackstone, Hellman & Friedman, Goldman Sachs, General Atlantic, Leonard Green & Partners, Apollo Global Management, GIC, and Sequoia Capital.\n\n\n\nWe're headquartered in SF with offices in NYC, Raleigh-Durham, and Dubai.\n\n\n\n\nTHE ROLE\n\nThis role is designed for former engineering leaders (IC or EM) or founders who are comfortable owning end-to-end technical outcomes but specifically want to continue being impactful as individual contributors and spend more time in the code.\n\n\n\nYou'll work on a small, high-caliber team (2–5 engineers and a PM) building AI products for our clients. You'll set technical direction, write code, and be the person the team looks to when something is hard.\n\n\n\nYou'll spend roughly 75% of your time in code and 25% working directly with clients — often their CTOs — understanding problems, walking through tradeoffs, and making sure what we’re building meets their needs.\n\n\n\nMost engineers take a decade to see this range of hard problems across this many domains. Here, you'll do it in your first year. To make this possible, we are religious about being the best company in the world to learn Applied AI engineering practices.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU BRING\n\n - 8+ years of engineering experience, with deep care for the craft. You've shipped multiple complete products end-to-end and write elegant, production-ready code across multiple disciplines.\n\n - Specific interest in applying software engineering fundamentals to AI systems. You care about balancing frontier model capabilities with good system design.\n\n - Comfort talking with senior technical stakeholders. You navigate conversations skillfully, and care about people using what you build.\n\n - High ownership mindset. You jump in without instruction, embrace a \"no job too big, no job too small\" mindset, and want to shape strategy and culture.\n\n - Low ego, high integrity. You help others and ask for help. You hold a high bar for honesty–with yourself and your team.\n   \n   \n\n\nOUR ENGINEERING PHILOSOPHY\n\nWe have a distinct approach to building AI systems: applying standard software engineering discipline to the non-deterministic world of frontier AI. We design systems around testable hypotheses, curate durable data sets, and ensure what we ship keeps working long after we've handed it over.\n\n\n\nAfter shipping 30+ AI products, we have strong opinions on what makes AI products succeed and how to get them into production. We think you'll find it refreshing if you've seen how most companies approach AI.\n\n\n\n\nHOW ODE IS DIFFERENT\n\nA typical engineer here ships two to three products per year and learns from dozens more. You have outsized autonomy on each product — but you won't have a year to polish a single system. The upside is constant time on the frontier of models and tooling, and a muscle for AI product development that's hard to build anywhere else.\n\n\n\nMost engineers look back at this as the biggest growth period of their career. But it's possible you won't like it — we recommend using the interview process to hear what our engineers think.\n\n\n\n\nOUR VALUES\n\n - Overdeliver: We are writing the playbook on how to create enterprise value with LLMs, and building our reputation as the world’s best applied AI team.\n\n - Overuse AI: We obsessively explore and experiment with Claude to push the frontier of applied AI and share what we learn with our teammates.\n\n - Over”engineer” the Culture: We’re building a culture that attracts and retains top applied AI talent, and we stress test large decisions through the perspective of our world class builders.\n   \n   \n\n\nLOCATION\n\nSan Francisco, CA\nNew York, NY\n\nWork Arrangement: 4 days in-person, Fridays remote\n\n\n\n\nBENEFITS\n\n - 🏦 Competitive Compensation Package: Attractive salary aligned with your experience and skills.\n\n - 📈 401k with Matching: Invest in your future with our company-matched retirement plan.\n\n - 🌴 Unlimited PTO: Take the time you need to relax and rejuvenate.\n\n - 🏥 Exceptional Medical, Dental, and Vision Coverage: Comprehensive health benefits to keep you and your family healthy.\n\n - 🚑 Health FSA: Manage out-of-pocket health expenses effectively.\n\n - 🚌 Commuter Benefits: Make your travel to work easier and more affordable.\n\n - 🏥 Life Insurance: Providing peace of mind for you and your loved ones.\n\n - 🎉 Team Events and Activities: Regular events to build camaraderie and a strong team spirit.\n\n\n\n\nREADY TO JOIN US?","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$275K – $400K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$275K - $400K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"898754f0-f78c-40c0-b0f4-6c12bf2a93c6","tierSummary":"The estimated total cash compensation range for this role is: $275K – $400K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"c3401b97-7242-4bcc-a3f3-4d62f4ac2958","summary":"The estimated total cash compensation range for this role is: $275K – $400K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":275000,"maxValue":400000},{"id":"52f39c9f-ee18-438e-8f1e-ddf16fce8a54","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":275000,"maxValue":400000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"0a382a4a-7bd9-435e-be98-cb2fa7465721","title":"Developer Relations Engineer","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco Office","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"New York Office","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York City "}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-05-25T19:18:28.891+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":false,"workplaceType":"OnSite","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/odewithanthropic/0a382a4a-7bd9-435e-be98-cb2fa7465721","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/odewithanthropic/0a382a4a-7bd9-435e-be98-cb2fa7465721/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>About Ode with Anthropic</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">How do you turn a decades-old dataset into an industry-leading medical coding agent? Teach an AI receptionist to book appointments in Spanish? Automatically generate working data connectors from API docs? Build agents that write, test, and deploy their own software packages?</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Anthropic is defining frontier AI. Ode is the team bringing frontier AI into practice.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are a team of experienced builders who care deeply about getting complex AI systems into production, with strong conviction about what makes them succeed. As Anthropic’s services venture, we tackle the hardest, most consequential AI problems for companies with real stakes, working closely with their Applied AI and Product teams to turn frontier technology into real world impact.<br /></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're backed by Anthropic, Blackstone, Hellman &amp; Friedman, Goldman Sachs, General Atlantic, Leonard Green &amp; Partners, Apollo Global Management, GIC, and Sequoia Capital.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're headquartered in SF with offices in NYC, Raleigh-Durham, and Dubai.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /></p><h1><strong>The Role</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ode is widely regarded by practitioners as one of the best teams at AI implementation in complex scenarios. Our brand awareness among top-tier engineers hasn't kept pace with our output. On May 20, we became the founding team of Anthropic's new AI Services Business, and it's the right moment to bring in our first Developer Relations Engineer to build a lasting engineering brand.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll be embedded in the engineering team, reading code, sitting in architecture reviews, talking to clients , and translating that work into content, community, and presence that engineers actually respect. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /></p><h2><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Write and publish technical content — blog posts, project teardowns, HN writeups — drawn from what the team is actually building</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build Ode's presence on channels where strong engineers spend time: Hacker News, technical podcasts, conferences, and niche communities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Run high-signal community touchpoints: dinners, workshops, small events where top engineers encounter Ode in a non-transactional context</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive open source contributions and external projects that reflect Ode's engineering caliber</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build partnerships with complementary technical brands — co-sponsoring events, co-publishing content, cross-pollinating communities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Feed signal back to engineering leadership: what practitioners are excited about, skeptical of, building toward<br /></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>What You Bring</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Strong engineering foundation. </strong>You've shipped software and cared about doing it right. You understand why good system design matters and can have a credible technical conversation with a senior engineer about AI architecture, eval design, or production tradeoffs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Exceptional writing. </strong>You write with clarity and specificity. You know the difference between content that earns attention and content that fills a feed. You've written things engineers have actually read and shared.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Taste for what resonates technically. </strong>You have a feel for the developer zeitgeist — what practitioners find credible, what reads as hype, what makes an HN post land versus get flagged.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>High ownership mindset. </strong>You jump in without instruction, embrace a \"no job too big, no job too small\" mindset, and want to shape strategy and culture from day one.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Low ego, high integrity. </strong>You help others and ask for help. You hold a high bar for honesty, with yourself and your team.<br /></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>Engineering at Ode</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br />We have a distinct approach to building AI systems: applying standard software engineering discipline to the non-deterministic world of frontier AI. We design systems around testable hypotheses, curate durable datasets, and ensure what we ship keeps working long after we've handed it over.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">After shipping 30+ AI products, we have strong opinions on what makes AI products succeed and how to get them into production. We think you'll find it refreshing if you've seen how most companies approach AI.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /></p><h1><strong>How Ode Is Different</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A typical engineer here ships two to three products per year and learns from dozens more. In this role, you'll have direct visibility into that full portfolio — which means a richer, more credible voice than any DevRel who's been handed a press release.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /></p><h1><strong>Our Values</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Overdeliver</strong>: We are writing the playbook on how to create enterprise value with LLMs, and building our reputation as the world’s best applied AI team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Overuse AI:</strong> We obsessively explore and experiment with Claude to push the frontier of applied AI and share what we learn with our teammates.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Over”engineer” the Culture: </strong>We’re building a culture that attracts and retains top applied AI talent, and we stress test large decisions through the perspective of our world class builders.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /></p></li></ul><h1><strong>Benefits</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">🏦 Competitive Compensation Package</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">📈 401k with Matching</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">🌴 Unlimited PTO</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">🏥 Exceptional Medical, Dental, and Vision Coverage</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">🚑 Health FSA</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">🚌 Commuter Benefits</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">🏥 Life Insurance</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">🎉 Team Events and Activities</p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT ODE WITH ANTHROPIC\n\n\n\nHow do you turn a decades-old dataset into an industry-leading medical coding agent? Teach an AI receptionist to book appointments in Spanish? Automatically generate working data connectors from API docs? Build agents that write, test, and deploy their own software packages?\n\n\n\nAnthropic is defining frontier AI. Ode is the team bringing frontier AI into practice.\n\n\n\nWe are a team of experienced builders who care deeply about getting complex AI systems into production, with strong conviction about what makes them succeed. As Anthropic’s services venture, we tackle the hardest, most consequential AI problems for companies with real stakes, working closely with their Applied AI and Product teams to turn frontier technology into real world impact.\n\n\nWe're backed by Anthropic, Blackstone, Hellman & Friedman, Goldman Sachs, General Atlantic, Leonard Green & Partners, Apollo Global Management, GIC, and Sequoia Capital.\n\n\n\nWe're headquartered in SF with offices in NYC, Raleigh-Durham, and Dubai.\n\n\n\n\n\nTHE ROLE\n\n\n\nOde is widely regarded by practitioners as one of the best teams at AI implementation in complex scenarios. Our brand awareness among top-tier engineers hasn't kept pace with our output. On May 20, we became the founding team of Anthropic's new AI Services Business, and it's the right moment to bring in our first Developer Relations Engineer to build a lasting engineering brand.\n\n\n\n\nYou'll be embedded in the engineering team, reading code, sitting in architecture reviews, talking to clients , and translating that work into content, community, and presence that engineers actually respect. \n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Write and publish technical content — blog posts, project teardowns, HN writeups — drawn from what the team is actually building\n\n - Build Ode's presence on channels where strong engineers spend time: Hacker News, technical podcasts, conferences, and niche communities\n\n - Run high-signal community touchpoints: dinners, workshops, small events where top engineers encounter Ode in a non-transactional context\n\n - Drive open source contributions and external projects that reflect Ode's engineering caliber\n\n - Build partnerships with complementary technical brands — co-sponsoring events, co-publishing content, cross-pollinating communities\n\n - Feed signal back to engineering leadership: what practitioners are excited about, skeptical of, building toward\n   \n   \n   \n\n\nWHAT YOU BRING\n\n - Strong engineering foundation. You've shipped software and cared about doing it right. You understand why good system design matters and can have a credible technical conversation with a senior engineer about AI architecture, eval design, or production tradeoffs.\n\n - Exceptional writing. You write with clarity and specificity. You know the difference between content that earns attention and content that fills a feed. You've written things engineers have actually read and shared.\n\n - Taste for what resonates technically. You have a feel for the developer zeitgeist — what practitioners find credible, what reads as hype, what makes an HN post land versus get flagged.\n\n - High ownership mindset. You jump in without instruction, embrace a \"no job too big, no job too small\" mindset, and want to shape strategy and culture from day one.\n\n - Low ego, high integrity. You help others and ask for help. You hold a high bar for honesty, with yourself and your team.\n   \n   \n   \n\n\nENGINEERING AT ODE\n\n\nWe have a distinct approach to building AI systems: applying standard software engineering discipline to the non-deterministic world of frontier AI. We design systems around testable hypotheses, curate durable datasets, and ensure what we ship keeps working long after we've handed it over.\n\n\n\nAfter shipping 30+ AI products, we have strong opinions on what makes AI products succeed and how to get them into production. We think you'll find it refreshing if you've seen how most companies approach AI.\n\n\n\n\n\nHOW ODE IS DIFFERENT\n\n\n\nA typical engineer here ships two to three products per year and learns from dozens more. In this role, you'll have direct visibility into that full portfolio — which means a richer, more credible voice than any DevRel who's been handed a press release.\n\n\n\n\n\nOUR VALUES\n\n\n\n - Overdeliver: We are writing the playbook on how to create enterprise value with LLMs, and building our reputation as the world’s best applied AI team.\n\n - Overuse AI: We obsessively explore and experiment with Claude to push the frontier of applied AI and share what we learn with our teammates.\n\n - Over”engineer” the Culture: We’re building a culture that attracts and retains top applied AI talent, and we stress test large decisions through the perspective of our world class builders.\n   \n   \n   \n\n\nBENEFITS\n\n🏦 Competitive Compensation Package\n\n📈 401k with Matching\n\n🌴 Unlimited PTO\n\n🏥 Exceptional Medical, Dental, and Vision Coverage\n\n🚑 Health FSA\n\n🚌 Commuter Benefits\n\n🏥 Life Insurance\n\n🎉 Team Events and Activities","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"d539bdad-0d66-4366-9295-71ce890cfc50","title":"Senior Technical Recruiter","department":"Talent","team":"Talent","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco Office","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"New York Office","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York City "}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-08-04T05:14:04.442+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":false,"workplaceType":"OnSite","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/odewithanthropic/d539bdad-0d66-4366-9295-71ce890cfc50","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/odewithanthropic/d539bdad-0d66-4366-9295-71ce890cfc50/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1>About Ode with Anthropic</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">How do you turn a decades-old dataset into an industry-leading medical coding agent? Teach an AI receptionist to book appointments in Spanish? Automatically generate working data connectors from API docs? Build agents that write, test, and deploy their own software packages?</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Anthropic is defining frontier AI. Ode is the team bringing frontier AI into practice.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are a team of experienced builders who care deeply about getting complex AI systems into production, with strong conviction about what makes them succeed. As Anthropic’s services venture, we tackle the hardest, most consequential AI problems for companies with real stakes, working closely with their Applied AI and Product teams to turn frontier technology into real world impact.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're backed by Anthropic, Blackstone, Hellman &amp; Friedman, Goldman Sachs, General Atlantic, Leonard Green &amp; Partners, Apollo Global Management, GIC, and Sequoia Capital.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're headquartered in SF with offices in NYC, Raleigh-Durham, and Dubai.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>The Role</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our talent is our product. Customers choose Ode because we bring together elite engineers, product leaders, and commercial operators to build and deploy applied AI systems.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re building a team that makes Ode the best place to learn applied AI. As a member of our talent team, you’ll play a critical role in making that real — identifying and closing exceptional talent. Engineering hiring is core to the role, but you’ll have the opportunity to work across functions as we grow.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>What You'll Do</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own critical engineering searches.<br /></strong>Partner with engineering leaders to identify, engage, and hire exceptional software engineers across senior, staff, and principal levels. You'll own searches from strategy through close and play a meaningful role in building our engineering organization.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Partner with hiring managers.<br /></strong>Develop hiring strategies, advise on talent markets, calibrate interview quality, and become a trusted thought partner throughout the hiring process.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Raise the recruiting bar.<br /></strong>Share best practices, mentor teammates, and help strengthen hiring judgment across the recruiting team. You'll lead through influence, not title.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build better recruiting systems.<br /></strong>Continuously improve how we recruit through data, AI, experimentation, and thoughtful process design. Find leverage that helps the team move faster without lowering the hiring bar.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Help shape the future of recruiting at Ode.<br /></strong>Contribute to interviewer enablement, recruiting operations, sourcing strategy, and the systems that allow us to scale while maintaining exceptional hiring quality.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>What You Bring</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>4+ years of experience recruiting exceptional engineering talent.<br /></strong>You've stood up engineering recruiting functions and built foundational engineering teams in early-stage or high-growth environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Strong hiring judgment.<br /></strong>You know what exceptional talent looks like and can make thoughtful, evidence-based hiring decisions while earning trust from candidates, hiring managers, and interview teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Technical fluency.<br /></strong>You understand modern engineering organizations and can credibly engage with both candidates and engineering leaders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Leadership through influence.<br /></strong>You naturally elevate the people around you by sharing knowledge, mentoring teammates, and driving improvements, regardless of whether you have direct reports.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Builder mindset.<br /></strong>You enjoy improving systems, challenging existing processes, and using AI, automation, and data to make recruiting more effective.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>High ownership.<br /></strong>You move with urgency, follow through on commitments, and take responsibility for outcomes. You don't wait to be told what needs fixing—you identify opportunities and act.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>Our Values</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Overdeliver: We are writing the playbook on how to create enterprise value with LLMs, and building our reputation as the world’s best applied AI team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Overuse AI: We obsessively explore and experiment with Claude to push the frontier of applied AI and share what we learn with our teammates.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Over”engineer” the Culture: We’re building a culture that attracts and retains top applied AI talent, and we stress test large decisions through the perspective of our world class builders.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>Location</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">San Francisco, CA<br />New York, NY</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work Arrangement: 4 days in-person, Fridays remote</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1>Benefits</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">🏦 Competitive Compensation Package: Attractive salary aligned with your experience and skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">📈 401k with Matching: Invest in your future with our company-matched retirement plan.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">🌴 Unlimited PTO: Take the time you need to relax and rejuvenate.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">🏥 Exceptional Medical, Dental, and Vision Coverage: Comprehensive health benefits to keep you and your family healthy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">🚑 Health FSA: Manage out-of-pocket health expenses effectively.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">🚌 Commuter Benefits: Make your travel to work easier and more affordable.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">🏥 Life Insurance: Providing peace of mind for you and your loved ones.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">🎉 Team Events and Activities: Regular events to build camaraderie and a strong team spirit.</p></li></ul>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT ODE WITH ANTHROPIC\n\nHow do you turn a decades-old dataset into an industry-leading medical coding agent? Teach an AI receptionist to book appointments in Spanish? Automatically generate working data connectors from API docs? Build agents that write, test, and deploy their own software packages?\n\n\n\nAnthropic is defining frontier AI. Ode is the team bringing frontier AI into practice.\n\nWe are a team of experienced builders who care deeply about getting complex AI systems into production, with strong conviction about what makes them succeed. As Anthropic’s services venture, we tackle the hardest, most consequential AI problems for companies with real stakes, working closely with their Applied AI and Product teams to turn frontier technology into real world impact.\n\n\n\nWe're backed by Anthropic, Blackstone, Hellman & Friedman, Goldman Sachs, General Atlantic, Leonard Green & Partners, Apollo Global Management, GIC, and Sequoia Capital.\n\nWe're headquartered in SF with offices in NYC, Raleigh-Durham, and Dubai.\n\n\n\n\nTHE ROLE\n\nOur talent is our product. Customers choose Ode because we bring together elite engineers, product leaders, and commercial operators to build and deploy applied AI systems.\n\nWe’re building a team that makes Ode the best place to learn applied AI. As a member of our talent team, you’ll play a critical role in making that real — identifying and closing exceptional talent. Engineering hiring is core to the role, but you’ll have the opportunity to work across functions as we grow.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own critical engineering searches.\n   Partner with engineering leaders to identify, engage, and hire exceptional software engineers across senior, staff, and principal levels. You'll own searches from strategy through close and play a meaningful role in building our engineering organization.\n\n - Partner with hiring managers.\n   Develop hiring strategies, advise on talent markets, calibrate interview quality, and become a trusted thought partner throughout the hiring process.\n\n - Raise the recruiting bar.\n   Share best practices, mentor teammates, and help strengthen hiring judgment across the recruiting team. You'll lead through influence, not title.\n\n - Build better recruiting systems.\n   Continuously improve how we recruit through data, AI, experimentation, and thoughtful process design. Find leverage that helps the team move faster without lowering the hiring bar.\n\n - Help shape the future of recruiting at Ode.\n   Contribute to interviewer enablement, recruiting operations, sourcing strategy, and the systems that allow us to scale while maintaining exceptional hiring quality.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU BRING\n\n - 4+ years of experience recruiting exceptional engineering talent.\n   You've stood up engineering recruiting functions and built foundational engineering teams in early-stage or high-growth environments.\n\n - Strong hiring judgment.\n   You know what exceptional talent looks like and can make thoughtful, evidence-based hiring decisions while earning trust from candidates, hiring managers, and interview teams.\n\n - Technical fluency.\n   You understand modern engineering organizations and can credibly engage with both candidates and engineering leaders.\n\n - Leadership through influence.\n   You naturally elevate the people around you by sharing knowledge, mentoring teammates, and driving improvements, regardless of whether you have direct reports.\n\n - Builder mindset.\n   You enjoy improving systems, challenging existing processes, and using AI, automation, and data to make recruiting more effective.\n\n - High ownership.\n   You move with urgency, follow through on commitments, and take responsibility for outcomes. You don't wait to be told what needs fixing—you identify opportunities and act.\n\n\n\n\nOUR VALUES\n\n - Overdeliver: We are writing the playbook on how to create enterprise value with LLMs, and building our reputation as the world’s best applied AI team.\n\n - Overuse AI: We obsessively explore and experiment with Claude to push the frontier of applied AI and share what we learn with our teammates.\n\n - Over”engineer” the Culture: We’re building a culture that attracts and retains top applied AI talent, and we stress test large decisions through the perspective of our world class builders.\n\n\n\n\nLOCATION\n\nSan Francisco, CA\nNew York, NY\n\nWork Arrangement: 4 days in-person, Fridays remote\n\n\n\n\nBENEFITS\n\n - 🏦 Competitive Compensation Package: Attractive salary aligned with your experience and skills.\n\n - 📈 401k with Matching: Invest in your future with our company-matched retirement plan.\n\n - 🌴 Unlimited PTO: Take the time you need to relax and rejuvenate.\n\n - 🏥 Exceptional Medical, Dental, and Vision Coverage: Comprehensive health benefits to keep you and your family healthy.\n\n - 🚑 Health FSA: Manage out-of-pocket health expenses effectively.\n\n - 🚌 Commuter Benefits: Make your travel to work easier and more affordable.\n\n - 🏥 Life Insurance: Providing peace of mind for you and your loved ones.\n\n - 🎉 Team Events and Activities: Regular events to build camaraderie and a strong team spirit.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$150K – $200K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$150K - $200K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"e6479a58-735b-412e-a996-f71f558dfe7d","tierSummary":"$150K – $200K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"66145f0a-9f90-4ece-9c18-c0d60377516e","summary":"$150K – $200K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":150000,"maxValue":200000},{"id":"c33dde8c-7e49-4e9b-b27d-cfafed6557ea","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":150000,"maxValue":200000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"950a2e5a-3658-491c-8a98-3a546f0df9a6","title":"Head of Business Operations and Analytics","department":"Business Operations","team":"Business Operations","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco Office","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-21T23:38:21.169+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/odewithanthropic/950a2e5a-3658-491c-8a98-3a546f0df9a6","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/odewithanthropic/950a2e5a-3658-491c-8a98-3a546f0df9a6/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>About Ode with Anthropic</strong><br /></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">How do you turn a decades-old dataset into an industry-leading medical coding agent? Teach an AI receptionist to book appointments in Spanish? Automatically generate working data connectors from API docs? Build agents that write, test, and deploy their own software packages?<br /><br /></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Anthropic is defining frontier AI. Ode is the team bringing frontier AI into practice.<br /><br /></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are a team of experienced builders who care deeply about getting complex AI systems into production, with strong conviction about what makes them succeed. As Anthropic’s services venture, we tackle the hardest, most consequential AI problems for companies with real stakes, working closely with their Applied AI and Product teams to turn frontier technology into real world impact.<br /><br /></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're backed by Anthropic, Blackstone, Hellman &amp; Friedman, Goldman Sachs, General Atlantic, Leonard Green &amp; Partners, Apollo Global Management, GIC, and Sequoia Capital.<br /><br /></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're headquartered in SF with offices in NYC, Raleigh-Durham, and Dubai.<br /><br /></p><h1><strong>The Role</strong><br /></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're hiring a seasoned Operator to lead and grow our lean Business Operations and Analytics team from first principles.<br /></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The core mandate: build the systems, infrastructure and enabling process to stay one step ahead of scale while taking on the special projects to support step-wise changes in our growth.<br /><br /></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ode is a true operations business: creating value by optimizing supply and demand. You’d own this critical intersection that’s the core of our business while writing the playbook for scaling in an AI native way.<br /><br /></p><h1><strong>What you'll do:</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build the infrastructure to scale:</strong> Build the systems, data, and processes that keep us ahead of growth. Approach internal operations like a product, using AI and automation to create better ways of working as we scale.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Lead critical strategic initiatives: </strong>Take on the cross-functional problems and opportunities that matter most to our next stage of growth—from new market expansion to new bets across the business.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Optimize supply and demand:</strong> Connect our commercial pipeline to our workforce through forecasting, capacity planning, and staffing—ensuring we have the right talent deployed against the right work while optimizing utilization and economics.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Drive company planning and performance:</strong> Own the rhythms that help us run the company—from annual and quarterly planning to internal communications, business reviews, and Board preparation.<br /><br /></p></li></ul><h1><strong>What you bring:</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You've scaled a high-growth business: </strong>You've helped build the systems and infrastructure behind a company through a period of rapid growth.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You bring exceptional analytical and technical rigor: </strong>You're highly quantitative, understand how data and systems work under the hood, and can build rigorous models from messy inputs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You're a player-coach:</strong> You can build and lead an exceptional team while staying deeply in the work.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You build lean by design: </strong>You default to better systems, automation, and AI before adding people or process.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You want to win:</strong> You have a high bar, move with urgency, and are deeply motivated to build something exceptional.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Our Values</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Overdeliver</strong>: We are writing the playbook on how to create enterprise value with LLMs, and building our reputation as the world’s best applied AI team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Overuse AI:</strong> We obsessively explore and experiment with Claude to push the frontier of applied AI and share what we learn with our teammates.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Over “engineer” the Culture: </strong>We’re building a culture that attracts and retains top applied AI talent, and we stress test large decisions through the perspective of our world class builders.</p></li></ul>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT ODE WITH ANTHROPIC\n\n\nHow do you turn a decades-old dataset into an industry-leading medical coding agent? Teach an AI receptionist to book appointments in Spanish? Automatically generate working data connectors from API docs? Build agents that write, test, and deploy their own software packages?\n\n\n\nAnthropic is defining frontier AI. Ode is the team bringing frontier AI into practice.\n\n\n\nWe are a team of experienced builders who care deeply about getting complex AI systems into production, with strong conviction about what makes them succeed. As Anthropic’s services venture, we tackle the hardest, most consequential AI problems for companies with real stakes, working closely with their Applied AI and Product teams to turn frontier technology into real world impact.\n\n\n\nWe're backed by Anthropic, Blackstone, Hellman & Friedman, Goldman Sachs, General Atlantic, Leonard Green & Partners, Apollo Global Management, GIC, and Sequoia Capital.\n\n\n\nWe're headquartered in SF with offices in NYC, Raleigh-Durham, and Dubai.\n\n\n\n\nTHE ROLE\n\n\nWe're hiring a seasoned Operator to lead and grow our lean Business Operations and Analytics team from first principles.\n\n\n\n\nThe core mandate: build the systems, infrastructure and enabling process to stay one step ahead of scale while taking on the special projects to support step-wise changes in our growth.\n\n\n\nOde is a true operations business: creating value by optimizing supply and demand. You’d own this critical intersection that’s the core of our business while writing the playbook for scaling in an AI native way.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO:\n\n - Build the infrastructure to scale: Build the systems, data, and processes that keep us ahead of growth. Approach internal operations like a product, using AI and automation to create better ways of working as we scale.\n\n - Lead critical strategic initiatives: Take on the cross-functional problems and opportunities that matter most to our next stage of growth—from new market expansion to new bets across the business.\n\n - Optimize supply and demand: Connect our commercial pipeline to our workforce through forecasting, capacity planning, and staffing—ensuring we have the right talent deployed against the right work while optimizing utilization and economics.\n\n - Drive company planning and performance: Own the rhythms that help us run the company—from annual and quarterly planning to internal communications, business reviews, and Board preparation.\n   \n   \n\n\nWHAT YOU BRING:\n\n - You've scaled a high-growth business: You've helped build the systems and infrastructure behind a company through a period of rapid growth.\n\n - You bring exceptional analytical and technical rigor: You're highly quantitative, understand how data and systems work under the hood, and can build rigorous models from messy inputs.\n\n - You're a player-coach: You can build and lead an exceptional team while staying deeply in the work.\n\n - You build lean by design: You default to better systems, automation, and AI before adding people or process.\n\n - You want to win: You have a high bar, move with urgency, and are deeply motivated to build something exceptional.\n   \n   \n\n\n\n\nOUR VALUES\n\n - Overdeliver: We are writing the playbook on how to create enterprise value with LLMs, and building our reputation as the world’s best applied AI team.\n\n - Overuse AI: We obsessively explore and experiment with Claude to push the frontier of applied AI and share what we learn with our teammates.\n\n - Over “engineer” the Culture: We’re building a culture that attracts and retains top applied AI talent, and we stress test large decisions through the perspective of our world class builders.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}}],"apiVersion":"1"}